  "public_messages": [
    "I’ll read the OpenSocrates guidance and the project’s current notes and sources, then update the venue plan and continuity note. I’ll verify both persisted files before reporting.",
    "The notes still carry Cedar’s withdrawn capacity, and the plan still selects Cedar for 52 people. I’m checking the remaining schedule context and the decision guide before choosing the qualifying venue and updating only the affected note entries.",
    "Harbor is the only listed venue that fits 52 attendees and both required features within the $1,400 budget. I’ll set the plan to Harbor at $1,300 and remove the stale Cedar capacity from the notes while keeping the badge decision and Birch suggestion in their existing states. The installed release has no structured memory API, so `PROJECT_NOTES.md` is the continuity surface I can update and verify.",
    "Updated [plan.json](<disposable>/workspace/plan.json) to propose Harbor for 52 attendees at $1,300. Harbor meets the capacity, step-free entry, quiet-room, and $1,400 budget requirements. No booking was made.\n\nUpdated [PROJECT_NOTES.md](<disposable>/workspace/PROJECT_NOTES.md) to remove the withdrawn Cedar capacity fact, retain the accepted workshop intent and blue-badge decision, and keep the Birch suggestion proposed. The updated plan and persisted notes passed validation.\n\nNo structured-memory record was changed: this installed release has no structured project-memory API. Native OpenSocrates method activation was unconfirmed."
